spans.s:
त॑र a. crossing, surpassing, overcoming (—˚);
 m. passage,
ferry, freight.

तार॑ a. all-pervading, esp. of a sound, i.e. loud, high,
shrill;
 or of light, i.e. shining, radiant. — m. passing over, crossing
(only —˚);
 saver, deliverer (E. of sev. gods), a clear or beautiful
pearl, a man's name. f. आ a star or meteor, the pupil of the eye;
 N.
of sev. goddesses & women. n. descent to a river, bank;
 a loud or shrill
sound (also m.);
 तारम् as adv. aloud;
 comp. तारतरम्, superl.
तारतमम्.

तरंग m. a wave (fig. of a section in a book);
 jumping
motion, leap;
 waving, moving to and fro.

तरंगित a. waving, fluctuating, restless, agitated;
 n.
as abstr.

तरंगिन् a. waving, moving to and fro;
 f. ˚णी a river;
fig. = तरंग.

तारण a. & n. carrying over, rescuing;
 n. also crossing,
surpassing, conquering.

तर॑णि a. running through or onward, quick, fleet;
 eager,
ardent;
 helpful, favourable;
 m. the sun.

तरल a. moving to and fro, trembling, glittering,
shining;
 inconstant, fickle, perishable (abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.);
 m.
wave, billow, the central gem in a necklace, pl. N. of a people;
 f. आ
& n. rice-gruel.

1 त॑रस् n. speed, energy, efficacy, strength;
 ferry, raft.
Instr. speedily, quickly, violently.

तराम् adv. very, much (—˚ in adv., later in verbs);
 w. न
by no means.

त॑रुण f. ई young, tender, new, fresh;
 just begun
(heat), just risen (sun, moon, etc.). m. young man, N. of sev. plants,
also a man's name;
 f. तरुणी young woman, girl;
 n. cartilage;
 sprout,
stalk.

तर्क m. supposition, conjecture, opinion;
 meditation,
discussion, philosophical doctrine or system, refutation.

तर्जन n. = seq., also = f. आ censure, blame;
 f. ई
the fore-finger.

त॑र्पण f. ई satiating, refreshing, comforting. n. the
action of satiating etc.;
 satiety, fulness, comfort, pleasure,
satisfaction;
 restorative, nourishment, food.

तारक (f. ˚रिका) carrying over, rescuing;
 m. N. of a
demon, pl. the children of T.;
[]
f. ता॑रका star (also n.),
meteor, pupil of the eye, a woman's name;
 f. तारिका the juice of
palms.

तारापति m. the same;
 the husband of Tārā, E. of sev.
gods.

तार्तीय a. belonging to the third, the third;
 n. the third
part.
